lesson: 131
title: The times table in stories
level: primary-2
stars: 0
explain: When there are several equal groups, multiply the number of groups by the number in one group.
explain: 4 bags with 6 apples in each bag hold 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 = 4 × 6 = 24 apples.
explain: It does not matter whether we say «4 groups of 6» or «6 in each of 4 groups»: the answer is 4 × 6.
vars: a=name t=thing k=2..9 m=2..9
answer: k * m
exercise: {a} has {k} bags with {m} {t} in each bag. How many {t} does {a} have?
exercise: There are {k} plates on the table. Each plate holds {m} {t}. How many {t} are there in all?
exercise: {a} buys {k} packs of {t}. There are {m} {t} in a pack. How many {t} does {a.he} buy?
exercise: A box has {k} rows of {t} with {m} {t} in each row. How many {t} are in the box?
exercise: {k} children each bring {m} {t} to school. How many {t} do they bring altogether?
exercise: {a} puts {m} {t} into each of {k} baskets. How many {t} does {a.he} put in the baskets?
test: Each of {k} friends got {m} {t} from {a}. How many {t} did {a} give away?
test: How many {t} fill {k} jars, if every jar takes {m}?
test: {a} lays out the {t} in {k} equal piles of {m}. How many {t} are laid out?
test: On each of {k} shelves there are {m} {t}. Count all the {t} on the shelves.
exercise: How many {t} are there altogether, if {a} has {k} bags and every bag holds {m} {t}?
exercise: {k} bags, {m} {t} per bag. How many {t} in total?
exercise: At a school fair in Ohio, {a} fills {k} paper cups with {m} {t} apiece. How many {t} does {a.he} use in all?
exercise: {a} has {k.words} boxes, and there are {m.words} {t} in every box. How many {t} are there in total?
exercise: In a classroom in Dublin there are {k} tables, and {m} {t} lie on each table. How many {t} are on the tables combined?
exercise: {m} {t} go into each of {k} lunch boxes. How many {t} go into the lunch boxes altogether?
exercise: {a} makes {k} gift bags for a party in Toronto and puts {m} {t} in every one. How many {t} are in the gift bags together?
exercise: There are {m} {t} in one tin. How many {t} are there in {k} tins?
test: A shop in Melbourne sells {t} in packets of {m}. {a} takes home {k} packets. What is the total number of {t}?
test: {k} times {m} {t}: how many {t} is that?
test: Grandma in Wellington hands each of her {k} grandchildren {m} {t}. How many {t} does she hand out in all?
test: How many {t} does {a} need to fill {k.words} trays with {m.words} {t} on each tray?
test: Every one of the {k} tents at a camp in Montana got {m} {t}. Altogether, how many {t} were given to the tents?
test: {a} counts {m} {t} in a row, and there are {k} such rows. Find the number of {t}.
exercise: {a} got {k+1} bags — no sorry, {k} bags, {m} {t} in each. how many {t} altogether
exercise: {k} packs of {t}, {m} in a pack, oh and the shop had like 50 packs left. how many {t} {a} got then
exercise: my brother says {k} bags of {m} {t} is {k*m+m}. nah thats wrong innit, how many {t} really
exercise: {a} has {k} boxes with {m} {t} in em. how many {t} {a.he} got
test: each of {k} mates brung {m} {t}, how many {t} we got
test: {m} {t} per plate, {k+2} plates — wait no, {k} plates. total {t}?
test: teacher wrote {k} × {m} = {k*m-1}?? cant be right. how many {t} in {k} rows of {m}
exam: It is given that {a} is in possession of {k} bags, each containing {m} {t}. Determine the aggregate quantity of {t}.
exam: Whereas {k} plates are placed upon a table and each plate bears {m} {t}, ascertain the total number of {t}.
exam: {a} purchases {k.words} packs of {t}, each pack comprising {m.words} {t}. State the number of {t} so purchased.
exam: Compute the product of {k} and {m}.
exercise: Grandma passed away and left {k} jars, with {m} buttons in each jar. How many buttons did she leave?
exercise: Since Dad was laid off, the family buys in bulk: {k} packs with {m} sausages in each pack. How many sausages is that?
test: {k} boxes "fell off the back of a lorry", yeah right, nicked more like. {m} {t} in each. how many
